diff --git a/docs/architecture/durable-session-journal.md b/docs/architecture/durable-session-journal.md
index 8fe5c0d..0000000 100644
--- a/docs/architecture/durable-session-journal.md
+++ b/docs/architecture/durable-session-journal.md
@@ -17,6 +17,8 @@ A normal persistence boundary is:
 3. append a full snapshot commit record bound to the complete event prefix, then flush it;
 4. atomically rewrite the compatibility session JSON.
 
+Runtime restart recovery uses this same boundary when interrupted plan steps are marked failed; it never updates only the compatibility JSON.
+
 The journal snapshot is authoritative over the compatibility JSON because it is committed first. State-only mutations are also committed as snapshot records, so recovery is not limited to fields represented by event payloads.
